After going 25000 turns without finding any sort of bag,
then finding a wand of wishing (0:2) just before the Quest,
I decided I'd play this game bagless, just for fun, and to
spite the RNG that gave me two random wands of wishing in a
single weekend.  I highly recommend this conduct to people
who think Gehennom should be made more...interesting. :)

--Many things were left unidentified since identify scrolls
would usually get burned up on the way to the nearest altar,
and usually I didn't have enough room to carry all the unIDed
stuff with me.  This meant I never identified the scroll of
genocide, meaning I couldn't nix Lh;.  Not killing ; meant
I had to wear my amulet of ESP in place of reflection when
crossing watery areas.  Which led to several unfortunate
accidents involving exploding wands.  Thankfully, my wand
of wishing was spared.

--I had to do the ascension run without holy water since
all my holy water got frozen by purple liches or burned up in
fire traps.  I had to go through half of Gehennom without
a pick-axe (since it was cursed and I had no way to uncurse
it).  At some point I wished for a horn of plenty (fruit
juice potions => more holy water), but it only came with 20
or so charges, so it was pretty useless.  Gehennom was
definitely the hardest and most frustrating part of the game,
just because of the fire traps.

--I was lucky enough to find a coaligned temple right before
Medusa's level, so I set up a stash there and returned to it
every five seconds (except I mapped Gehennom downside-up, so
I had to leave a lot of stuff from there behind).

--For whatever reason, I was rarely burdened, except in
the early game.  I made a lot of mistakes in the early game
(like trying on cursed boots of levitation after my pet died
and relying on a cursed ring of polymorph to get them off).

Having ascended a game without reflection and a game
without a bag, I must say I now prefer the BoH ending
to Sokoban.  Less equipment destruction. =P

Thanks to the people in #nethack, who were really awesome
and helpful.

